        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bfa3b0dc-a936-5377-a034-c241eeebb097",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fannie Lee Chaney, James Earl Chaney\n- Organizations: Ku Klux Klan\n- Events: Freedom Summer, 1964 murders of civil rights workers\n- Places: Meridian, Mississippi, Philadelphia, Mississippi\n- Roles: baker, civil rights activist, civil rights worker\n\nFacts:\n- James Earl Chaney was born on May 30, 1943, and he was from Meridian, Mississippi.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney was born on September 4, 1921, and she was an American baker.\n- On June 21, 1964, civil rights worker James Earl Chaney was one of three American civil rights workers murdered by members of the Ku Klux Klan near Philadelphia, Mississippi, during Freedom Summer.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney became a civil rights activist after her son James Chaney was murdered by the Ku Klux Klan during the 1964 Freedom Summer rides in Mississippi.\n- Fannie Lee Chaney died on May 22, 2007.",
